Literature sweep completed 2026-05-04.

Effector identification:
- PWT3 is an avirulence effector from Pyricularia oryzae (barley and Lolium blast
  pathotypes, isolate Br58 = Ao-type functional form). Signal peptide 1-18; mature
  chain 19-141 = 123 residues (UniProt A0A223ZP76; B-type from Br48).
- PWT3 is NOT a MAX-fold effector by sequence: Inoue et al. 2017 Science state it
  "lacked similarity to known proteins or protein domains." Le Naour-Vernet 2023
  PLoS Pathog classifies it as "non-MAX effector." This contradicts the prior
  knowledge for the campaign.
- The natural resistance gene Rwt3 is a CC-NLR without HMA integrated domain
  (Arora et al. 2023 Nat Plants). PWT3 is not naturally recognised via HMA.
- GenBank: LC202650-LC202657 (Ao/Atm/B types from various isolates; Inoue 2017).
- No deposited PDB structure for PWT3.

Source PDB and numbering convention:
- Chain A: AF3 monomer prediction of Pikp-1 HMA (UniProt E9KPB5, residues 186-263),
  renumbered 1-78 (pipeline = literature - 185). Shared with all pikp1_* campaigns.
- Chain B: AF3 monomer prediction of PWT3 Ao-type mature chain (DDBJ LC202650 or
  equivalent; ~123 residues after signal peptide cleavage at ~residue 18-20).
  Rung 6 of the fallback ladder. REQUIRES FOLD VALIDATION before complex assembly.
- Complex template: 6G10 (Pikp-HMA/AVR-PikD, De la Concepcion 2018) — CONDITIONAL
  on AF3 PWT3 monomer confirming a MAX-like β-sandwich fold (pLDDT >70, RMSD to
  2MYW < 3 Å over ≥40 residues).
- Fallback (Scenario B): AF3-multimer of Pikp-1 HMA + PWT3 Ao-type mature chain
  (rung 7). Must be run regardless as cross-check.

Primary contig (CONDITIONAL on MAX-fold assumption):
  A1-32/12-20/A50-68/8-14 B
  (Flex regions: Interface 2 pipeline ~33-49, Interface 3 pipeline ~69-78.)
  This contig MUST be revised if AF3 shows non-MAX fold or different binding face.

Campaign-blocker status:
- SOFT BLOCKER: AF3 monomer prediction of PWT3 must be run and validated before
  complex assembly can be finalised. The MAX-fold assumption may not hold.
- If non-MAX (Scenario B): AF3-multimer required; §4 and §6 of the report must be
  redone from the multimer contact map.

Primary papers cited:
- Inoue et al. 2017 Science (PWT3 cloning; "no functional domains"; sequence)
- Inoue et al. 2021 New Phytologist (PWT4 biology; confirms PWT3 = no domains)
- Arora et al. 2023 Nature Plants (Rwt3 = CC-NLR, no HMA)
- Le Naour-Vernet et al. 2023 PLoS Pathog (PWT3 = non-MAX effector)
- Maqbool 2015 eLife (Pikp-1 HMA scaffold; 5A6W)
- De la Concepcion 2018 Nat Plants (6G10; Interface 1/2/3 definition)
- Kanzaki 2012 Plant Journal (AVR-Pik alleles)
- Longya 2019 MPMI (AVR-PikF; Interface 3)

